# Everything the images must not see. The build contexts for ops/deploy/Dockerfile.{api,client} are the
# repo root, so a missing entry here means it is copied into a layer and then into the registry — including
# `node_modules` (a 400 MB layer that also breaks `npm ci` reproducibility) and any wallet keypair.
.git
.github
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite
**/target
**/test-ledger
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-wal
**/*.sqlite-shm
**/*-keypair.json
**/id.json
# SEC-B55: `**/.env` is one name out of the five Vite reads — for `vite build` (mode production) it loads
# `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.production` and `.env.production.local` from the client root, and every one of
# them can set any `VITE_*` name. process.env wins for the names the Dockerfile declares, so a stray
# undeclared switch (VITE_API_MOCK, VITE_FLAG_DEBUG_PANEL, …) is copied in and baked into a production
# bundle without appearing in any diff of the deploy artifacts. `client/.env.example` literally tells
# developers to "copy to .env.local", so that file is expected to exist on a working machine.
**/.env*
!**/.env.example
ops/deploy/secrets
ops/deploy/backup/*
!ops/deploy/backup/.gitkeep
anchor-clean
coverage
docs
test-results
playwright-report
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/
dapp-store/
guttercaps-landing.html
